{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls6_jpg\\eng\\131.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "Vocabulary", "conf": 0.891, "box": [[142, 191], [347, 203], [345, 244], [139, 232]]}, {"text": "1 Find the synonyms of the given words from a dictionary and use them each in a", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[82, 266], [1113, 268], [1113, 305], [81, 303]]}, {"text": "sentence.", "conf": 0.831, "box": [[121, 304], [248, 307], [247, 331], [120, 328]]}, {"text": "words", "conf": 0.824, "box": [[151, 357], [240, 354], [241, 386], [152, 388]]}, {"text": "synonyms", "conf": 0.834, "box": [[376, 361], [505, 359], [506, 387], [377, 389]]}, {"text": "sentences", "conf": 0.891, "box": [[779, 361], [901, 361], [901, 385], [779, 385]]}, {"text": "tranquil", "conf": 0.884, "box": [[151, 404], [255, 402], [256, 437], [152, 439]]}, {"text": "vagrant", "conf": 0.809, "box": [[153, 454], [254, 454], [254, 485], [153, 485]]}, {"text": "beckon", "conf": 0.72, "box": [[153, 496], [250, 499], [249, 531], [152, 528]]}, {"text": "blessing", "conf": 0.805, "box": [[151, 542], [261, 547], [259, 582], [150, 577]]}, {"text": "doom", "conf": 0.799, "box": [[151, 592], [232, 592], [232, 623], [151, 623]]}, {"text": "eventide", "conf": 0.794, "box": [[152, 643], [264, 640], [265, 668], [153, 671]]}, {"text": "2 Paraphrase the poem in your own words.", "conf": 0.905, "box": [[76, 700], [646, 705], [646, 735], [75, 730]]}, {"text": "3 Write an objective summary of the poem in no more than 40 words. Remember", "conf": 0.901, "box": [[74, 749], [1112, 762], [1112, 794], [73, 782]]}, {"text": "to write it in your own words. Remember, you do not have to add in your views.", "conf": 0.888, "box": [[116, 785], [1113, 797], [1113, 826], [116, 814]]}, {"text": "Just summarise what the poet is saying.", "conf": 0.887, "box": [[114, 813], [633, 824], [632, 857], [113, 846]]}, {"text": "Use of Language", "conf": 0.876, "box": [[134, 890], [440, 903], [438, 943], [133, 930]]}, {"text": "A gerund is a noun formed from a verb. All gerunds end in -ing. As they are nouns,", "conf": 0.868, "box": [[76, 992], [1052, 1011], [1052, 1043], [75, 1025]]}, {"text": "gerunds can function as one of the following:", "conf": 0.912, "box": [[74, 1034], [634, 1045], [633, 1081], [73, 1070]]}, {"text": "The Subject of a Verb.", "conf": 0.892, "box": [[77, 1079], [372, 1086], [371, 1116], [76, 1109]]}, {"text": "Example:", "conf": 0.865, "box": [[77, 1125], [190, 1125], [190, 1156], [77, 1156]]}, {"text": "The labouring hours suit my spirit. (labouring' is the subject of the verb 'suit')", "conf": 0.92, "box": [[74, 1165], [997, 1185], [996, 1217], [73, 1197]]}, {"text": "The Object of a Verb.", "conf": 0.894, "box": [[77, 1209], [360, 1217], [359, 1247], [76, 1239]]}, {"text": "Example:", "conf": 0.888, "box": [[75, 1253], [191, 1255], [190, 1289], [74, 1287]]}, {"text": "Ienjoy traveling the market-place.", "conf": 0.896, "box": [[73, 1297], [508, 1305], [507, 1338], [72, 1330]]}, {"text": "(\"traveling\" is the direct object of the verb \"enjoy.\")", "conf": 0.919, "box": [[76, 1341], [701, 1352], [700, 1384], [75, 1373]]}, {"text": "The Object of a Preposition", "conf": 0.869, "box": [[77, 1384], [447, 1390], [447, 1423], [76, 1416]]}, {"text": "Example:", "conf": 0.861, "box": [[77, 1426], [191, 1431], [190, 1466], [75, 1461]]}, {"text": "I surprised them by working in the field and in the forest.", "conf": 0.911, "box": [[75, 1471], [768, 1480], [768, 1513], [74, 1504]]}, {"text": "(\"working\" is the object of the preposition \"by.\")", "conf": 0.937, "box": [[78, 1514], [669, 1523], [668, 1556], [77, 1547]]}, {"text": "NOTFORSALE", "conf": 0.865, "box": [[345, 1627], [545, 1627], [545, 1652], [345, 1652]]}, {"text": "124", "conf": 0.7, "box": [[609, 1621], [663, 1621], [663, 1660], [609, 1660]]}, {"text": "awaz e inqilab.com", "conf": 0.904, "box": [[479, 1708], [761, 1708], [761, 1741], [479, 1741]]}]}